{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "Blah Blob",
  "script": "-- Due to an emulation glitch with Mini vMac's Macintosh II\n-- emulation, sin and cos only give accurate answers between\n-- 0 and π/2. The following functions work around this issue:\n\nfunction toRad x\nreturn x * pi / 180\nend toRad\n\nfunction sinFrom0To180 x\nif x ≤ 45 then\nreturn sin(toRad(x))\nend if\n\nif x ≤ 90 then\nreturn cos(toRad(90-x))\nend if\n\nif x ≤ 135 then\nreturn cos(toRad(x-90))\nend if\n\nif x ≤ 180 then\nreturn sin(toRad(180-x))\nend if\n\nreturn 0\nend sinFrom0To180\n\nfunction realSin x\nrepeat while x < 0\nadd 360 to x\nend repeat\n\nput x mod 360 into x\n\nif x ≤ 180 then\nreturn sinFrom0To180(x)\nend if\n\nreturn -sinFrom0To180(x-180)\nend realSin\n\nfunction realCos x\nreturn realSin(x+90)\nend realCos\n\nfunction lerp u, a, b\nif u ≤ 0 then\nreturn a\nend if\n\nif u ≥ 1 then\nreturn b\nend if\n\nreturn round((b-a) * u + a)\nend lerp\n\nfunction clamp val, minVal, maxVal\nreturn max(min(val, maxVal), minVal)\nend clamp\n\nfunction getCurrentControls\nput empty into controls\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to 7\nput (button i of card \"settings\") & \",\" ¬\n& short name of button i of card \"settings\" into line i of controls\nend repeat\n\nreturn controls\nend getCurrentControls\n\nfunction gameCyclesToTime cycleCount\nput (cycleCount mod 30) into cycles\nput cycleCount div 30 into totalSeconds\nput totalSeconds mod 60 into seconds\nput totalSeconds div 60 into totalMinutes\nput totalMinutes mod 60 into minutes\nput totalMinutes div 60 into hours\n\nif the number of chars of cycles = 1 then\nput \"0\" before cycles\nend if\nif the number of chars of seconds = 1 then\nput \"0\" before seconds\nend if\nif the number of chars of minutes = 1 then\nput \"0\" before minutes\nend if\n\nif hours = 0 then\nreturn minutes & \":\" & seconds & \".\" & cycles\nelse\nreturn hours & \":\" & minutes & \":\" & seconds & \".\" & cycles\nend if\nend gameCyclesToTime\n\nfunction getSpeedrunModeEnabled\nreturn hilite of button id 11 of card \"settings\"\nend getSpeedrunModeEnabled\n\nfunction maxLevelPlayed\nreturn max(1, card field \"maxLevelPlayed\" of card \"game\")\nend maxLevelPlayed\n\nfunction levelNumberOfLevelName levelName\nput card field \"_levelOrder\" of card \"levels\" into levelOrder\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of lines of levelOrder\nif levelName = line i of levelOrder then\nreturn i\nend if\nend repeat\n\nreturn empty\nend levelNumberOfLevelName\n\nfunction levelDisplayNameForLevelName levelName\nreturn item 1 of card field (levelName & \"_name\") of card \"levels\"\nend levelDisplayNameForLevelName\n\nfunction shortLevelDisplayNameForLevelName levelName\nput card field (levelName & \"_name\") of card \"levels\" into levelNames\nif the number of items of levelNames > 1 then\nreturn item 2 of levelNames\nelse\nput item 1 of levelNames into fullName\nrepeat\nput offset(return, fullName) into returnIndex\nif returnIndex = 0 then exit repeat\nput space into char returnIndex of fullName\nend repeat\nreturn fullName\nend if\nend shortLevelDisplayNameForLevelName\n\nfunction levelNameForLevelNumber levelNum\nreturn line levelNum of card field \"_levelOrder\" of card \"levels\"\nend levelNameForLevelNumber\n\n------ High score stuff ------\n\nfunction getRankForTime type, cycleCount\nput card field (type & \"_data\") of card \"data\" into dataList\nput number of lines of dataList into rankCount\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to rankCount\nif cycleCount ≤ item 3 of line i of dataList then\nreturn i\nend if\nend repeat\n\nreturn rankCount + 1\nend getRankForTime\n\nfunction getDescendingRankForDeaths deaths\nput card field \"deathsDec_data\" of card \"data\" into dataList\nput number of lines of dataList into rankCount\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to rankCount\nif deaths ≥ item 1 of line i of dataList then\nreturn i\nend if\nend repeat\n\nreturn rankCount + 1\nend getDescendingRankForDeaths\n\nfunction getAscendingRankForDeaths listType, deaths\nif deaths = 0 then\nreturn 1\nend if\n\nput card field (listType & \"_data\") of card \"data\" into dataList\nput number of lines of dataList into rankCount\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to rankCount\nif deaths ≤ item 1 of line i of dataList then\nreturn i\nend if\nend repeat\n\nreturn rankCount + 1\nend getAscendingRankForDeaths\n\nfunction ranksInList type\nreturn the number of lines of card field (type & \"_data\") of card \"data\"\nend ranksInList\n\nfunction nameForRank type, rank\nreturn line rank of card field (type & \"_names\") of card \"data\"\nend nameForRank\n\nfunction deathsForRank type, rank\nreturn item 1 of line rank of card field (type & \"_data\") of card \"data\"\nend deathsForRank\n\nfunction winsForRank type, rank\nreturn item 2 of line rank of card field (type & \"_data\") of card \"data\"\nend winsForRank\n\nfunction timeForRank type, rank\nreturn item 3 of line rank of card field (type & \"_data\") of card \"data\"\nend timeForRank\n\nfunction startLevelForRank type, rank\nreturn item 4 of line rank of card field (type & \"_data\") of card \"data\"\nend startLevelForRank\n\nfunction endLevelForRank type, rank\nreturn item 5 of line rank of card field (type & \"_data\") of card \"data\"\nend endLevelForRank\n\nfunction limitTo100Entries dataList\nrepeat while the number of lines of dataList > 100\ndelete last line of dataList\nend repeat\n\nrepeat while last char of dataList = return\ndelete last char of dataList\nend repeat\n\nreturn dataList\nend limitTo100Entries\n\non addGameHighScoreEntry listType, rank, theName, ¬\nstartLevel, endLevel, deathCount, winCount, cycleCount, ¬\nlevelDeaths, levelWins, levelTimes\n\nif rank > 100 then\nexit addGameHighScoreEntry\nend if\n\nput card field (listType & \"_names\") of card \"data\" into nameList\nput card field (listType & \"_data\") of card \"data\" into dataList\nput card field (listType & \"_levelDeaths\") of card \"data\" into levelDeathsList\nput card field (listType & \"_levelWins\") of card \"data\" into levelWinsList\nput card field (listType & \"_levelTimes\") of card \"data\" into levelTimesList\n\nput deathCount & \",\" & winCount & \",\" & cycleCount & \",\" ¬\n& startLevel & \",\" & endLevel into data\n\nput the number of lines of dataList into rankCount\n\nif rank > rankCount then\nput theName before line rank of nameList\nput data before line rank of dataList\nput levelDeaths before line rank of levelDeathsList\nput levelWins before line rank of levelWinsList\nput levelTimes before line rank of levelTimesList\nelse\nput theName & return before line rank of nameList\nput data & return before line rank of dataList\nput levelDeaths & return before line rank of levelDeathsList\nput levelWins & return before line rank of levelWinsList\nput levelTimes & return before line rank of levelTimesList\nend if\n\nput limitTo100Entries(nameList) into nameList\nput limitTo100Entries(dataList) into dataList\nput limitTo100Entries(levelDeathsList) into levelDeathsList\nput limitTo100Entries(levelWinsList) into levelWinsList\nput limitTo100Entries(levelTimesList) into levelTimesList\n\nput nameList into card field (listType & \"_names\") of card \"data\"\nput dataList into card field (listType & \"_data\") of card \"data\"\nput levelDeathsList into card field (listType & \"_levelDeaths\") of card \"data\"\nput levelWinsList into card field (listType & \"_levelWins\") of card \"data\"\nput levelTimesList into card field (listType & \"_levelTimes\") of card \"data\"\nend addGameHighScoreEntry\n\non addSingleLevelHighScoreEntry listType, rank, theName, ¬\ndeathCount, winCount, cycleCount\n\nif rank > 100 then\nexit addSingleLevelHighScoreEntry\nend if\n\nput card field (listType & \"_names\") of card \"data\" into nameList\nput card field (listType & \"_data\") of card \"data\" into dataList\nput deathCount & \",\" & winCount & \",\" & cycleCount into data\n\nput the number of lines of dataList into rankCount\n\nif rank > rankCount then\nput theName before line rank of nameList\nput data before line rank of dataList\nelse\nput theName & return before line rank of nameList\nput data & return before line rank of dataList\nend if\n\nput limitTo100Entries(nameList) into nameList\nput limitTo100Entries(dataList) into dataList\n\nput nameList into card field (listType & \"_names\") of card \"data\"\nput dataList into card field (listType & \"_data\") of card \"data\"\nend addSingleLevelHighScoreEntry\n\n---- End of high score stuff -----\n\n\n---- Music stuff\n\nfunction isMusicEnabled\nreturn hilite of button id 4 of card \"settings\"\nend isMusicEnabled\n\nfunction isMusicPlaying\nglobal currentMusic\nreturn currentMusic is not empty\nend isMusicPlaying\nfunction isBackgroundMusicPlaying\nglobal currentMusic\nreturn isMusicPlaying() and currentMusic = \"background music\"\nend isBackgroundMusicPlaying\n\nfunction isTitleMusicPlaying\nglobal currentMusic\nreturn isMusicPlaying() and currentMusic = \"title music\"\nend isTitleMusicPlaying\n\non playMusic musicName, volume\nglobal currentMusic, currentMusicVolume\n-- Songs play on their own channel, looping, beside sound effects.\nif not isMusicEnabled() then\nexit playMusic\nend if\nif currentMusic = musicName then\nexit playMusic\nend if\nstopMusic\nplay musicName\nput musicName into currentMusic\nput volume into currentMusicVolume\nend playMusic\non playBackgroundMusic\nplayMusic \"background music\", 50\nend playBackgroundMusic\n\non playTitleMusic\nplayMusic \"title music\", 38\nend playTitleMusic\n\non stopMusic\nglobal currentMusic\nif currentMusic is not empty then\nplay stop currentMusic\nput empty into currentMusic\nend if\nend stopMusic\non fadeOutMusicInTicks fadeTime\nstopMusic\nend fadeOutMusicInTicks\non fadeOutMusic\nstopMusic\nend fadeOutMusic\non maybeResumeMusic\nglobal currentMusic, pausedMusic\nif not isMusicEnabled() or currentMusic is not empty or ¬\npausedMusic is empty then exit maybeResumeMusic\nplayMusic pausedMusic, 50\nend maybeResumeMusic\n\n-- Around the win dialog: the song stops, then starts again.\non pauseMusic\nglobal currentMusic, pausedMusic\nput currentMusic into pausedMusic\nstopMusic\nend pauseMusic\n\non resumeMusic\nglobal pausedMusic\nif pausedMusic is not empty then playMusic pausedMusic, 50\nput empty into pausedMusic\nend resumeMusic\n\n-- Which of these keys (by name, as the keysDown names them) are held\n-- down: true or false for each.\nfunction checkKeys keyList\nput \",\" & the keysDown & \",\" into held\nput empty into states\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of items of keyList\nput item i of keyList into k\nput k is not empty and (\",\" & k & \",\") is in held into item i of states\nend repeat\nreturn states\nend checkKeys\n\n-- The first key held down that isn't Shift, Option, Command or Control.\nfunction firstKeyDown\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of items of the keysDown\nget item i of the keysDown\nif (\",\" & it & \",\") is not in \",shift,option,command,control,\" then return it\nend repeat\nreturn empty\nend firstKeyDown\n---- End music stuff\n\n---- Data stuff\n\nfunction openDataFile\nput dataFilePath() into filePath\nopen file filePath\n\nif the result = \"File is already open.\" then\nclose file filePath\nopen file filePath\nend if\n\nif the result is not empty then\nanswer \"An error occurred while writing Blah Blob's data:\" & return & the result\nreturn empty\nend if\n\nreturn filePath\nend openDataFile\n\non readAppData\nput openDataFile() into filePath\nif filePath is empty then exit readAppData\n\nreadAppDataFromFile filePath\nclose file filePath\nend readAppData\n\nfunction readAppDataBlock filePath, blockName, allowMissing\nread from file filePath until formfeed\nput it into block\n\nif block is empty or last char of block ≠ formfeed then\nif allowMissing then\nreturn empty\nelse\nanswer \"Blah Blob's settings file is invalid!\" & return & ¬\n\"Reason: the block for \" & blockName & \" appears to be missing\"\nreturn formfeed & \"error\" & formfeed\nend if\nend if\n\ndelete last char of block\nreturn block\nend readAppDataBlock\n\non readAppDataFromFile filePath\nglobal volumeLevelFromSettings\nput formfeed & \"error\" & formfeed into errorSignal\n\nif the result is not empty then\nanswer \"An error occurred while reading Blah Blob's data:\" & return & the result\nexit readAppDataFromFile\nend if\n\nread from file filePath until formfeed\nput it into settingsVersion\n\nif settingsVersion = empty then\n-- No settings file, so nothing to do\nexit readAppDataFromFile\nend if\n\nif last char of settingsVersion ≠ formfeed then\nanswer \"Blah Blob's settings file is invalid!\" & return & ¬\n\"Reason: Invalid data\"\nexit readAppDataFromFile\nend if\n\ndelete last char of settingsVersion\n\nif settingsVersion is not a number ¬\nor settingsVersion < 1 or settingsVersion > 3 then\nanswer \"Blah Blob's settings file is invalid!\" & return & ¬\n\"Reason: Bad version number\"\nexit readAppDataFromFile\nend if\n\nput readAppDataBlock(filePath, \"settings\", false) into settings\nif settings = errorSignal then exit readAppDataFromFile\n\nput validateSettings(settings) into validation\nif validation ≠ true then\nanswer \"Blah Blob's settings file is invalid!\" & return & ¬\n\"Reason: \" & validation\nexit readAppDataFromFile\nend if\n\nif settingsVersion ≥ 2 then\nput readAppDataBlock(filePath, \"maxLevel\", false) into maxLevel\n\nif settings = errorSignal then\nexit readAppDataFromFile\nend if\n\nif maxLevel is not a number ¬\nor maxLevel < 1 or maxLevel > 21 then\nput 1 into maxLevel\nexit readAppDataFromFile\nend if\nelse\n-- Forgot to include this originally... whoops!\nput 21 into maxLevel\nend if\n\nif settingsVersion ≥ 3 then\nput readAppDataBlock(filePath, \"maxLevel\", false) into volumeLevel\n\nif settings = errorSignal then\nexit readAppDataFromFile\nend if\n\nif volumeLevel is not a number ¬\nor volumeLevel < 0 or volumeLevel > 7 then\nput 6 into volumeLevel\nend if\nelse\nput 6 into volumeLevel\nend if\n\nput \"deathsAsc,deathsDec,speedruns\" into listTypes\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of items of listTypes\nput item i of listTypes into listType\n\ndo \"put readAppDataBlock(filePath, \" & listType & \"_names, false) into temp\"\nif temp = errorSignal then exit readAppDataFromFile\ndo \"put temp into \" & listType & \"_names\"\n\ndo \"put readAppDataBlock(filePath, \" & listType & \"_data, false) into temp\"\nif temp = errorSignal then exit readAppDataFromFile\ndo \"put temp into \" & listType & \"_data\"\n\ndo \"put readAppDataBlock(filePath, \" & listType & \"_levelDeaths, false) into temp\"\nif temp = errorSignal then exit readAppDataFromFile\ndo \"put temp into \" & listType & \"_levelDeaths\"\n\ndo \"put readAppDataBlock(filePath, \" & listType & \"_levelWins, false) into temp\"\nif temp = errorSignal then exit readAppDataFromFile\ndo \"put temp into \" & listType & \"_levelWins\"\n\ndo \"put readAppDataBlock(filePath, \" & listType & \"_levelTimes, false) into temp\"\nif temp = errorSignal then exit readAppDataFromFile\ndo \"put temp into \" & listType & \"_levelTimes\"\nend repeat\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to 21\n-- The original beta of the game only had 20 levels! So we're\n-- cheesing it here to make sure those settings still load\nput (i = 21) into allowMissing\ndo \"put readAppDataBlock(filePath, level\" & i & \"_names, \" & allowMissing & \") into temp\"\nif temp = errorSignal then exit readAppDataFromFile\ndo \"put temp into level\" & i & \"_names\"\n\ndo \"put readAppDataBlock(filePath, level\" & i & \"_data, \" & allowMissing & \") into temp\"\nif temp = errorSignal then exit readAppDataFromFile\ndo \"put temp into level\" & i & \"_data\"\nend repeat\n\nput readAppDataBlock(filePath, \"deathsExtra_names\", true) into deathsExtra_names\nput readAppDataBlock(filePath, \"deathsExtra_data\", true) into deathsExtra_data\n\n-- Okay, looks like things are good!\n\nsetSettingsFromData settings\n\nput maxLevel into card field \"maxLevelPlayed\" of card \"game\"\nput volumeLevel into volumeLevelFromSettings\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of items of listTypes\nput item i of listTypes into listType\n\ndo \"put \" & listType & \"_names into card field \" & quote & listType ¬\n& \"_names\" & quote & \" of card \" & quote & \"data\" & quote\ndo \"put \" & listType & \"_data into card field \" & quote & listType ¬\n& \"_data\" & quote & \" of card \" & quote & \"data\" & quote\ndo \"put \" & listType & \"_levelDeaths into card field \" & quote & listType ¬\n& \"_levelDeaths\" & quote & \" of card \" & quote & \"data\" & quote\ndo \"put \" & listType & \"_levelWins into card field \" & quote & listType ¬\n& \"_levelWins\" & quote & \" of card \" & quote & \"data\" & quote\ndo \"put \" & listType & \"_levelTimes into card field \" & quote & listType ¬\n& \"_levelTimes\" & quote & \" of card \" & quote & \"data\" & quote\nend repeat\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to 21\ndo \"put level\" & i & \"_names into card field \" & quote & \"level\" & i ¬\n& \"_names\" & quote & \" of card \" & quote & \"data\" & quote\ndo \"put level\" & i & \"_data into card field \" & quote & \"level\" & i ¬\n& \"_data\" & quote & \" of card \" & quote & \"data\" & quote\nend repeat\n\nput deathsExtra_names into card field \"deathsExtra_names\" of card \"data\"\nput deathsExtra_data into card field \"deathsExtra_data\" of card \"data\"\nend readAppDataFromFile\n\non writeAppData\nput openDataFile() into filePath\nif filePath is empty then exit writeAppData\n\nwriteAppDataToFile filePath\nclose file filePath\nend writeAppData\n\non writeAppDataToFile filePath\nwrite \"3\" & formfeed to file filePath\nwrite settingsToData() & formfeed to file filePath\nwrite maxLevelPlayed() & formfeed to file filePath\nwrite the soundVolume & formfeed to file filePath\n\nput \"deathsAsc,deathsDec,speedruns\" into listTypes\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of items of listTypes\nput item i of listTypes into listType\nwrite (card field (listType & \"_names\") of card \"data\") & formfeed to file filePath\nwrite (card field (listType & \"_data\") of card \"data\") & formfeed to file filePath\nwrite (card field (listType & \"_levelDeaths\") of card \"data\") & formfeed to file filePath\nwrite (card field (listType & \"_levelWins\") of card \"data\") & formfeed to file filePath\nwrite (card field (listType & \"_levelTimes\") of card \"data\") & formfeed to file filePath\nend repeat\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to 21\nput \"level\" & i into listType\nwrite (card field (listType & \"_names\") of card \"data\") & formfeed to file filePath\nwrite (card field (listType & \"_data\") of card \"data\") & formfeed to file filePath\nend repeat\n\nwrite (card field \"deathsExtra_names\" of card \"data\") & formfeed to file filePath\nwrite (card field \"deathsExtra_data\" of card \"data\") & formfeed to file filePath\nend writeAppDataToFile\n\nfunction settingsToData\nput hilite of button \"speedrun mode\" of card \"settings\" into speedrun\nput hilite of button \"show frames per second\" of card \"settings\" into showFPS\nput hilite of button \"Sound FX\" of card \"settings\" into enableSound\nput hilite of button \"Music\" of card \"settings\" into enableMusic\nput card field \"controls\" of card \"game\" into controls\nput short name of button 1 of card \"settings\" into leftControlName\nput short name of button 2 of card \"settings\" into rightControlName\nput short name of button 3 of card \"settings\" into bounceControlName\nput short name of button 4 of card \"settings\" into explodeControlName\nput short name of button 5 of card \"settings\" into pauseControlName\nput short name of button 7 of card \"settings\" into winControlName\nput short name of button 6 of card \"settings\" into resetControlName\nput word 2 of the selectedLine of button \"frame limit\" of card \"settings\" into frameLimitType\n\nreturn speedrun & return & ¬\nshowFps & return & ¬\nenableSound & return & ¬\nenableMusic & return & ¬\ncontrols & return & ¬\nleftControlName & return & ¬\nrightControlName & return & ¬\nbounceControlName & return & ¬\nexplodeControlName & return & ¬\npauseControlName & return & ¬\nwinControlName & return & ¬\nresetControlName & return & ¬\nframeLimitType\nend settingsToData\n\non setSettingsFromData data\nset hilite of button \"speedrun mode\" of card \"settings\" to line 1 of data\nset hilite of button \"show frames per second\" of card \"settings\" to line 2 of data\nset hilite of button \"Sound FX\" of card \"settings\" to line 3 of data\nset hilite of button \"Music\" of card \"settings\" to line 4 of data\nput line 5 of data into card field \"controls\" of card \"game\"\nset name of button 1 of card \"settings\" to line 6 of data\nset name of button 2 of card \"settings\" to line 7 of data\nset name of button 3 of card \"settings\" to line 8 of data\nset name of button 4 of card \"settings\" to line 9 of data\nset name of button 5 of card \"settings\" to line 10 of data\nset name of button 7 of card \"settings\" to line 11 of data\nset name of button 6 of card \"settings\" to line 12 of data\nselect line (line 13 of data) of button \"frame limit\" of card \"settings\"\nend setSettingsFromData\n\nfunction validateSettings data\nif the number of lines of data ≠ 13 then\nreturn \"App settings has wrong number of lines\"\nend if\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to 4\nif line i of data ≠ \"true\" and line i of data ≠ \"false\" then\nreturn \"Line\" && i && \"of app settings is invalid\"\nend if\nend repeat\n\nif the number of items of line 5 of data ≠ 7 then\nreturn \"Wrong number of control keycodes\"\nend if\n\nif line 13 of data ≠ \"1\" and line 13 of data ≠ \"2\" and line 13 of data ≠ \"3\" then\nreturn \"Invalid frame rate setting\"\nend if\n\nreturn true\nend validateSettings\n\nfunction dataFilePath\n-- A plain name is a file in the stack's folder.\nreturn \"Blah Blob Data\"\nend dataFilePath\n---- End data stuff\n\non openStack\nglobal kioskMode, volumeLevelFromSettings\nset the textArrows to true\n\nput false into kioskMode\n\n-- On a screen the card's size, the menu bar would cover it.\nif item 3 of the screenRect - item 1 of the screenRect = 512 ¬\nand item 4 of the screenRect - item 2 of the screenRect = 342 then\nhide menubar\nend if\n\nif the userLevel = 2 then\nreset menuBar\ncleanUI\nend if\n\nput 6 into volumeLevelFromSettings\nreadAppData\n\nif volumeLevelFromSettings is a number then\nset the soundVolume to volumeLevelFromSettings\nend if\nend openStack\n\non closeStack\nglobal resetGameForDistribution\ncloseMusic\n\nif resetGameForDistribution ≠ true then\nwriteAppData\nend if\nend closeStack\n\non idle\nglobal cleanedMenus\n\nif cleanedMenus = true and the userLevel > 2 then\nreset menuBar\nput false into cleanedMenus\nend if\nend idle\n\non flushAllEvents\nflush keys\n-- For some reason FlushEvents is not enough to prevent accidental\n-- clicks, so we do this too:\nget the mouse\nend flushAllEvents\n\non closeMusic\nif isMusicPlaying() then\nfadeOutMusicInTicks 45\nend if\nend closeMusic\n\non quit\nglobal kioskMode\n\n-- (Kiosk mode shut the Mac down here.)\nend quit\n\non suspendStack\ncloseMusic\nend suspendStack\n\non keyDown theKey\nglobal cleanedUI\n\nif cleanedUI ≠ true then pass keyDown\nif the selectedField = \"message box\" then pass keyDown\n\nif there is not a card field \"highscoreNameField\" then\nexit keyDown\nend if\n\nif visible of card field \"highscoreNameField\" = true then\npass keyDown\nend if\nend keyDown\n\non cleanUI\nglobal cleanedUI\nput true into cleanedUI\ncleanMenus\nend cleanUI\n\non maybeDeleteMenu menuName\nif there is a menu menuName then delete menu menuName\nend maybeDeleteMenu\n\non maybeDeleteMenuItem menuItemName, menuName\nif there is a menuItem menuItemName of menu menuName then\ndelete menuItem menuItemName of menu menuName\nend if\nend maybeDeleteMenuItem\n\non cleanMenus\nglobal cleanedMenus\nput true into cleanedMenus\n\nreset menuBar\nmaybeDeleteMenu \"Edit\"\nmaybeDeleteMenu \"Go\"\nmaybeDeleteMenu \"Tools\"\nmaybeDeleteMenu \"Objects\"\nmaybeDeleteMenu \"Font\"\nmaybeDeleteMenu \"Style\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"New Stack...\", \"File\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"Open Stack...\", \"File\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"Close Stack\", \"File\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"Save A Copy...\", \"File\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"Compact Stack\", \"File\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"Delete Stack...\", \"File\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"Page Setup...\", \"File\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"Print Field...\", \"File\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"Print Card\", \"File\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"Print Stack...\", \"File\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"Print Report...\", \"File\"\nmaybeDeleteMenuItem \"Quit HyperCard\", \"File\"\n\nif there is a menuItem \"-1\" of menu \"File\" then\ndelete menuItem \"-1\" of menu \"File\"\nend if\n\nif there is a menuItem \"-2\" of menu \"File\" then\ndelete menuItem \"-2\" of menu \"File\"\nend if\n\nif there is a menuItem \"-3\" of menu \"File\" then\ndelete menuItem \"-3\" of menu \"File\"\nend if\n\nput \"Quit Blah Blob\" after menu \"File\" with menuMessages \"quitGame\"\nend cleanMenus\n\non quitGame\ndoMenu \"Quit HyperCard\"\nend quitGame\n\non help\nend help\n\non openCard\nglobal playingGame\nif playingGame = true then\nplay stop\nplay \"boing\"\nset lockMessages to true\ngo to card \"game\"\nset lockMessages to false\nend if\nend openCard\n\non findInScripts text\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of cards\nif text is in script of card i then\nanswer the long name of card i with \"Stop\" or \"Continue\"\nif it is \"Stop\" then exit to HyperCard\nend if\nput 1 into j\nrepeat while there is a button j of card i\nif text is in script of button j of card i then\nanswer the long name of button j of card i with \"Stop\" or \"Continue\"\nif it is \"Stop\" then exit to HyperCard\nend if\nadd 1 to j\nend repeat\nput 1 into j\nrepeat while there is a card field j of card i\nif text is in script of card field j of card i then\nanswer the long name of card field j of card i with \"Stop\" or \"Continue\"\nif it is \"Stop\" then exit to HyperCard\nend if\nadd 1 to j\nend repeat\nend repeat\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of backgrounds\nif text is in script of background i then\nanswer the long name of background i with \"Stop\" or \"Continue\"\nif it is \"Stop\" then exit to HyperCard\nend if\nput 1 into j\nrepeat while there is a bg button j of card i\nif text is in script of bg button j of card i then\nanswer the long name of bg button j of card i with \"Stop\" or \"Continue\"\nif it is \"Stop\" then exit to HyperCard\nend if\nadd 1 to j\nend repeat\nput 1 into j\nrepeat while there is a bg field j of card i\nif text is in script of bg field j of card i then\nanswer the long name of bg field j of card i with \"Stop\" or \"Continue\"\nif it is \"Stop\" then exit to HyperCard\nend if\nadd 1 to j\nend repeat\nend repeat\nif text is in script of this stack then\nanswer \"Stack!\"\nend if\nend findInScripts",
  "width": 512,
  "height": 342,
  "next_id": 12169,
  "backgrounds": [
    {
      "id": 2568,
      "name": "gameBackground",
      "script": "-- connection data:\n-- 1: switch positions\n-- 2: current switch state and original switch state\n-- 3: closed left moving doors\n-- 4: open left moving doors\n-- 5: closed up moving doors\n-- 6: open up moving doors\n-- 7: closed right moving doors\n-- 8: open right moving doors\n-- 9: closed down moving doors\n-- 10: open down moving doors\n-- 11: on button positions\n-- 12: off button positions\n\nfunction inBackground\nreturn the checkMark of menuItem \"Background\" of menu \"Edit\"\nend inBackground\n\non goIntoBackground\nif inBackground() then exit goIntoBackground\ndoMenu \"Background\"\nend goIntoBackground\n\non goOutOfBackground\nif not inBackground() then exit goOutOfBackground\ndoMenu \"Background\"\nend goOutOfBackground\n\non ensureLevelObjectsCreatedForLevel levelName, setStyle, setVisible\nput false into justCreated\nput levelName & \"_map\" into mapName\n\nif there is no bg field mapName then\ngoIntoBackground\ndoMenu \"new field\"\nset name of last bg field to mapName\nput true into justCreated\nend if\nif setStyle or justCreated then\nset rect of bg field mapName to rect of card field levelName\nset textFont of bg field mapName to \"Sprites\"\nset textSize of bg field mapName to 16\nset dontWrap of bg field mapName to true\nset style of bg field mapName to \"scrolling\"\nset sharedText of bg field mapName to true\nend if\n\nset visible of bg field mapName to setVisible\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to 9\nput false into justCreated\nput levelName & \"_c\" & i into storageButtonName\n\nif there is no bg button storageButtonName then\ngoIntoBackground\ndoMenu \"new button\"\nset name of last bg button to storageButtonName\nput true into justCreated\nend if\nif setStyle or justCreated then\nset style of bg button storageButtonName to \"rect\"\nset showName of bg button storageButtonName to true\nput \"441,x,510,x\" into r\nput i*15 into item 2 of r\nput (i+1)*15 into item 4 of r\nset rect of bg button storageButtonName to r\nset textFont of bg button storageButtonName to \"geneva\"\nset textSize of bg button storageButtonName to 9\nend if\n\nset visible of bg button storageButtonName to setVisible\nend repeat\n\nend ensureLevelObjectsCreatedForLevel\n\non ensureLevelObjectsCreated setStyle, setVisible\ngo to card \"levels\"\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of card fields\nput short name of card field i into levelName\nif \"_\" is in levelName then next repeat\n\nensureLevelObjectsCreatedForLevel levelName, setStyle, setVisible\nend repeat\n\ngoOutOfBackground\nchoose \"browse\" tool\nend ensureLevelObjectsCreated\n\nfunction processHorizontalDoor data\nput empty into processed\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of words of data\nput word i of data into door\nput item 1 of door into x\nput item 2 of door into y\nput false into foundIt\n\nrepeat with j = 1 to the number of words of processed\nput word j of processed into doorRange\n\nif item 1 of doorRange ≠ y then\nnext repeat\nend if\n\nif item 3 of doorRange + 1 = x then\n-- The following two lines need to be separate steps due to\n-- a bug in HyperCard's text processing:\nput x into item 3 of doorRange\nput doorRange into word j of processed\nput true into foundIt\nexit repeat\nend if\nend repeat\n\nif not foundIt then\nif processed is not empty then\nput space & y & \",\" & x & \",\" & x after processed\nelse\nput y & \",\" & x & \",\" & x into processed\nend if\nend if\nend repeat\n\nreturn processed\nend processHorizontalDoor\n\nfunction processVerticalDoor data\nput empty into processed\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of words of data\nput word i of data into door\nput item 1 of door into x\nput item 2 of door into y\nput false into foundIt\n\nrepeat with j = 1 to the number of words of processed\nput word j of processed into doorRange\n\nif item 1 of doorRange ≠ x then\nnext repeat\nend if\n\nif item 3 of doorRange + 1 = y then\n-- The following two lines need to be separate steps due to\n-- a bug in HyperCard's text processing:\nput y into item 3 of doorRange\nput doorRange into word j of processed\nput true into foundIt\nexit repeat\nend if\nend repeat\n\nif not foundIt then\nif processed is not empty then\nput space & x & \",\" & y & \",\" & y after processed\nelse\nput x & \",\" & y & \",\" & y into processed\nend if\nend if\nend repeat\n\nreturn processed\nend processVerticalDoor\n\nfunction connectionStorageBgButtonName levelName, index\nreturn levelName & \"_c\" & index\nend connectionStorageBgButtonName\n\non processConnection levelName, index\nput connectionStorageBgButtonName(levelName, index) into storageName\n\nif word 2 of line 2 of bg button storageName = \"unset\" then\nput word 1 of line 2 of bg button storageName into ¬\nword 2 of line 2 of bg button storageName\nend if\n\n-- left doors\nput processHorizontalDoor(line 3 of bg button storageName) into doorData\nput doorData into line 3 of bg button storageName\nput processHorizontalDoor(line 4 of bg button storageName) into doorData\nput doorData into line 4 of bg button storageName\n\n-- up doors\nput processVerticalDoor(line 5 of bg button storageName) into doorData\nput doorData into line 5 of bg button storageName\nput processVerticalDoor(line 6 of bg button storageName) into doorData\nput doorData into line 6 of bg button storageName\n\n-- right doors\nput processHorizontalDoor(line 7 of bg button storageName) into doorData\nput doorData into line 7 of bg button storageName\nput processHorizontalDoor(line 8 of bg button storageName) into doorData\nput doorData into line 8 of bg button storageName\n\n-- down doors\nput processVerticalDoor(line 9 of bg button storageName) into doorData\nput doorData into line 9 of bg button storageName\nput processVerticalDoor(line 10 of bg button storageName) into doorData\nput doorData into line 10 of bg button storageName\nend processConnection\n\nfunction cleanMapData mapData\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of lines of mapData\nput line i of mapData into theLine\nput the number of chars of theLine into charCount\nif charCount ≤ 26 then\nnext repeat\nend if\n\nput 0 into lineEnd\nput 0 into c\nrepeat while lineEnd ≤ 26\nadd 1 to c\nif char c of theLine is not in \"123456789\" then\nadd 1 to lineEnd\nend if\nend repeat\n\nif c > charCount then next repeat\ndelete char c to charCount of line i of mapData\nend repeat\n\nreturn mapData\nend cleanMapData\n\non processLevelConnections levelName\nput card field levelName of card \"levels\" into mapData\nput cleanMapData(mapData) into mapData\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of lines of mapData\nif the number of chars of line i of mapData < 26 then\nanswer \"Line\" && i && \"does not have enough tiles!\" with \"oh no!\"\nexit processLevelConnections\nend if\nend repeat\n\nput return into connectionTemplate\nrepeat 12 times\nput return after connectionTemplate\nend repeat\n\nput \"false unset\" into line 2 of connectionTemplate\n\nput the itemDelimiter into orgItemDelimiter\n\nput \";:[{'\" & quote & \"/?\" into doorTiles\nput \"P p P p \" into doorTileReplacements\n\n-- Need to process all the connections in order\nput empty into connectionLocs\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to 9\nput return after connectionLocs\nput connectionStorageBgButtonName(levelName, i) into storageName\nput connectionTemplate into bg button storageName\nend repeat\n\nput 0 into blah\n\nrepeat forever\nadd 1 to blah\n--put blah\nset cursor to busy\nput \"0 65536\" into nextConnection\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to 9\nif line i of connectionLocs is empty then\nput offset(i, mapData) into c\nput c into line i of connectionLocs\nelse\nput line i of connectionLocs into c\nend if\n\nif c ≠ 0 and c < word 2 of nextConnection then\nput i && c into nextConnection\nend if\nend repeat\n\nput word 1 of nextConnection into connectionNum\n\nif connectionNum = 0 then\nexit repeat\nend if\n\nput word 2 of nextConnection into connectionLoc\nrepeat with i = 1 to 9\nif line i of connectionLocs ≠ 0 then\nsubtract 1 from line i of connectionLocs\nend if\nend repeat\nput empty into line connectionNum of connectionLocs\n\nput connectionStorageBgButtonName(levelName, connectionNum) into storageName\n\nput connectionLoc div 27 + 1 into y\nput connectionLoc mod 27 into x\ndelete char connectionLoc of mapData\nput char connectionLoc of mapData into tile\n\nif tile is in \"=+\" then\nput (tile = \"+\") into onStatus\n\nif word 2 of line 2 of bg button storageName ≠ \"unset\" and ¬\nword 2 of line 2 of bg button storageName ≠ onStatus then\nanswer \"Error! Switches on connection\" && connectionNum && \"out of sync!\"\nexit to HyperCard\nend if\n\nput onStatus && onStatus into line 2 of bg button storageName\nput x & \",\" & y & space after line 1 of bg button storageName\nnext repeat\nend if\n\nif tile is in \"Vv√◊\" then\nput x & \",\" & y & space after line 12 of bg button storageName\nnext repeat\nend if\n\nif tile is in \"Bb∫ı\" then\nput x & \",\" & y & space after line 11 of bg button storageName\nnext repeat\nend if\n\nrepeat with dir = 1 to 4\nif tile = char (dir*2-1) of doorTiles then\nput space & x & \",\" & y after line (dir*2+1) of bg button storageName\nput char (dir*2-1) of doorTileReplacements into char connectionLoc of mapData\nexit repeat\nend if\n\nif tile = char (dir*2) of doorTiles then\nput space & x & \",\" & y after line (dir*2+2) of bg button storageName\nput char (dir*2) of doorTileReplacements into char connectionLoc of mapData\nexit repeat\nend if\nend repeat\nend repeat\n\nrepeat with i = 1 to 9\nprocessConnection levelName, i\n\nput connectionStorageBgButtonName(levelName, i) into storageName\n\n-- left doors\nput line 3 of bg button storageName into doors\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of words of doors\nput \"…\" into char (item 2 of word i of doors) of ¬\nline (item 1 of word i of doors) of mapData\nend repeat\n\n-- up doors\nput line 5 of bg button storageName into doors\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of words of doors\nput \"“\" into char (item 1 of word i of doors) of ¬\nline (item 2 of word i of doors) of mapData\nend repeat\n\n-- right doors\nput line 7 of bg button storageName into doors\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of words of doors\nput \"æ\" into char (item 3 of word i of doors) of ¬\nline (item 1 of word i of doors) of mapData\nend repeat\n\n-- down doors\nput line 9 of bg button storageName into doors\nrepeat with i = 1 to the number of words of doors\nput \"÷\" into char (item 1 of word i of doors) of ¬\nline (item 3 of word i of doors) of mapData\nend repeat\nend repeat\n\nput mapData into bg field (levelName & \"_map\")\nend processLevelConnections\n\n\non initSounds\nglobal soundsInited, lastSplats, lastBigSplats, lastDeaths\nglobal lastSpringSounds, disableSound\nglobal firstSoundID, lastSoundID\n\n--if disableSound then exit initSounds\n\nput 128 into firstSoundID\nput 165 into lastSoundID\n\nput true into soundsInited\n\nif lastSplats is empty then\nput \"1,2,3,4,5,6\" into lastSplats\nend if\n\nif lastBigSplats is empty then\nput \"1,2,3,4,5,6\" into lastBigSplats\nend if\n\nif lastDeaths is empty then\nput \"1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\" into lastDeaths\nend if\n\nif lastSpringSounds is empty then\nput \"1,2,3,4,5,6\" into lastSpringSounds\nend if\nrepeat with i = firstSoundID to lastSoundID\nend repeat\n\n--answer \"sounds inited!\"\nend initSounds\n\non deinitSounds\nglobal soundsInited\nglobal firstSoundID, lastSoundID\n\nif soundsInited ≠ \"true\" then\nexit deinitSounds\nend if\n\nstopMovingPlatformFX\nif the result is true then\nexit deinitSounds\nend if\nrepeat with i = firstSoundID to lastSoundID\nend repeat\nput false into soundsInited\n--answer \"sounds deinited!\"\nend deinitSounds\n\non stopRepeatingSounds\nend stopRepeatingSounds\n\non playSplat\nglobal lastSplats, disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playSplat\n\nput random(4) into index\nput item index of lastSplats into newSFX\ndelete item index of lastSplats\nput \",\" & newSFX after lastSplats\nplay (\"splat\" & newSFX)\nend playSplat\n\non playBigSplat\nglobal lastBigSplats, disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playBigSplat\n\nput random(4) into index\nput item index of lastBigSplats into newSFX\ndelete item index of lastBigSplats\nput \",\" & newSFX after lastBigSplats\nplay (\"bigSplat\" & newSFX)\nend playBigSplat\n\non playDeathFX\nglobal lastDeaths, disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playDeathFX\n\nput random(3) into index\nput item index of lastDeaths into newSFX\ndelete item index of lastDeaths\nput \",\" & newSFX after lastDeaths\nplay (\"death\" & newSFX)\nend playDeathFX\n\non playSpringFX\nglobal lastSpringSounds, disableSound, cyclesSinceSpringSFX\nif disableSound or cyclesSinceSpringSFX < 3 then exit playSpringFX\n\n-- Sometimes several spring sound effects can be played\n-- rapidly within a few cycles, so cyclesSinceSpringSFX\n-- helps prevent that\nput 0 into cyclesSinceSpringSFX\nput random(3) into index\nput item index of lastSpringSounds into newSFX\ndelete item index of lastSpringSounds\nput \",\" & newSFX after lastSpringSounds\nplay (\"spring\" & newSFX)\nend playSpringFX\n\non playSlurpFX\nglobal disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playSlurpFX\nplay \"slurp\"\nend playSlurpFX\n\non playPopFX\nglobal disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playPopFX\nplay \"pop\"\nend playPopFX\n\non playCheckpointFX alternateChannels\nglobal disableSound, lastChannelForCheckpointFX\nif disableSound then exit playCheckpointFX\n\n-- alternateChannels will be true only for the very last\n-- bit of level 20\nif alternateChannels and lastChannelForCheckpointFX = \"three\" then\nplay \"checkpoint\"\nput \"four\" into lastChannelForCheckpointFX\nelse if alternateChannels and lastChannelForCheckpointFX = \"four\" then\nplay \"checkpoint\"\nput \"two\" into lastChannelForCheckpointFX\nelse\nplay \"checkpoint\"\nput \"three\" into lastChannelForCheckpointFX\nend if\nend playCheckpointFX\n\non playYay\nglobal disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playYay\nplay \"yay\"\nend playYay\n\non playButton1\nglobal disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playButton1\nplay \"button1\"\nend playButton1\n\non playButton2\nglobal disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playButton2\nplay \"button2\"\nend playButton2\n\non playLever1\nglobal disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playLever1\nplay \"lever1\"\nend playLever1\n\non playLever2\nglobal disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playLever2\nplay \"lever2\"\nend playLever2\n\non startMovingPlatformFX\nglobal disableSound, playingMovingPlatformFX\nif disableSound then exit startMovingPlatformFX\nplay \"movingPlatforms\"\nput true into playingMovingPlatformFX\nend startMovingPlatformFX\n\non stopMovingPlatformFX\nglobal disableSound, playingMovingPlatformFX\nif disableSound then exit stopMovingPlatformFX\nput false into playingMovingPlatformFX\nend stopMovingPlatformFX\n\non playSillyFanfare\nglobal disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playSillyFanfare\nplay \"fanfare\"\nend playSillyFanfare\n\non playKaChing\nglobal disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playKaChing\nplay \"ka-ching\"\nend playKaChing\n\non playCheer\nglobal disableSound\nif disableSound then exit playCheer\nplay \"cheer\"\nend playCheer\n\non timingStartFrame\nglobal startTimes, startTimesCount\n\nput the ticks into startTime\nput startTime & \",\" before startTimes\ndelete item startTimesCount+1 of startTimes\nend timingStartFrame\n\non timingEndFrameAndMaybeFrameLimit\nglobal startTimes, startTimesCount, multiFrameDt, multiFrameDtCount\nglobal showFPS, frameLimitType, showFPSCycles\nglobal blah\n\n-- Doing frame limiting is a bit tricky, since this game is\n-- likely to be running in Mini vMac which doesn't provide\n-- completely accurate timing information, especially if music\n-- is playing. So in the case of Mini vMac, we want to do\n-- something a little more complicated than waiting until the\n-- internal clock says that 2 ticks have elapsed since the\n-- start of a cycle. In BasiliskII, SheepShaver, and an actual\n-- PPC mac, this doesn't appear to be necessary.\n\n-- The solution for Mini vMac seems to be to keep track of the\n-- start times of the last 5-10 cycles, and then use that to\n-- get an accurate enough picture of how long we need to wait\n-- to keep things running at no more than 30 fps.\n\nif frameLimitType = \"Mini vMac\" then\n-- First, base our wait time on how long the last three\n-- cycles should last in order for the game to run at 30\n-- fps, rather than just looking at only the last cycle:\nput 3 into backFrames\nput item backFrames of startTimes into refTime\nput (2*backframes) - (the ticks-refTime) into waitTime\nput waitTime into waitTimeBefore\n\n-- That on its own works fairly well, but I observed that\n-- the above three lines on their own would keep the game\n-- running at around 26-27 fps, rather than 30. The following\n-- bit adjusts the wait times by looking at a larger duration\n-- and cutting the wait time down if we're lagging a bit. Even\n-- then the fps would still tend to hang steady around 29, so\n-- the numbers are fudged a bit by subtracting one from the\n-- number of frames we would have expected to have happened in\n-- that time. This seems to get us running at about as close to\n-- 30 fps exactly as we can get!\n\n--put 0 into adjustment\nput multiFrameDtCount*2 - 1 into expectedMultiFrameDt\nif multiFrameDt > expectedMultiFrameDt then\nput (multiFrameDt-expectedMultiFrameDt) into adjustment\nsubtract adjustment from waitTime\nend if\n\n-- if the number of chars of waitTimeBefore = 1 then\n-- put \" \" & waitTimeBefore into thing\n-- else\n-- put waitTimeBefore into thing\n-- end if\n\n-- if the number of chars of adjustment = 1 then\n-- put \"    \" & adjustment after thing\n-- else\n-- put \"   \" & adjustment after thing\n-- end if\n\n-- put \"    \" & waitTime after thing\n-- put thing\n\nif waitTime > 0 then\nwait waitTime\nend if\nelse if frameLimitType = \"Normal\" then\nput 2 - the ticks + item 1 of startTimes into waitTime\n\nif waitTime > 0 then\nwait waitTime\nend if\nend if\n\nput the ticks into endOfCycleTime\nput endOfCycleTime - item multiFrameDtCount of startTimes into multiFrameDt\n\nif showFPS then\nadd 1 to showFPSCycles\n\nif showFPSCycles = 10 then\nput endOfCycleTime - last item of startTimes into totalDt\nput endOfCycleTime - item 1 of startTimes into singleFrameDt\nput (60 * startTimesCount div totalDt) into fpsData\nput 0 into showFPSCycles\nset name of card button id 113 to fpsData\nend if\nend if\nend timingEndFrameAndMaybeFrameLimit\n\non timingReset\nglobal startTimes, startTimesCount, multiFrameDt, multiFrameDtCount\nglobal frameLimitType, showFPSCycles\n\n-- timing constants:\nput 10 into multiFrameDtCount\nput 60 into fpsFrames\n\nput the selectedText of button \"Frame limit\" of card \"settings\" ¬\ninto frameLimitType\nput 0 into multiFrameDt\nput max(multiFrameDtCount, fpsFrames) into startTimesCount\nput the ticks into startTime\nput 0 into showFPSCycles\n\nput startTime+2 into startTimes\nrepeat with i = 2 to startTimesCount\nput \",\" & startTime-i*2 after startTimes\nend repeat\nend timingReset\n",
      "parts": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "kind": "Field",
          "name": "test_map",
